      "writtenOn": "2018-06-18T21:35:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No - that\u0027s still possible and out-of-tree support shouldn\u0027t go away (at least I don\u0027t have a plan to ever remove it).\n\nWhat I meant when I wrote this is that we shouldn\u0027t support token providers that pass around dictionaries that end up being the actual token response (like what we used to do with the UUID/PKI/Fernet token providers). What I plan to do is simplify the token provider interface in a way that makes it simpler to maintain (and for external providers to implement), since external drivers shouldn\u0027t need to muck around or understand a massive token dictionary.\n\nI can reword this if you think it will make it more clear.",
